<Base title="Privacy policy" description="How PHP Hub handles personal data.">
<div class="page-prose"><h1>Privacy policy</h1>
<p><em>Last updated: 25 October 2026.</em></p>
<!-- TODO(Raghav): add a contact email for privacy requests and review this text before relying on it legally. -->
<h2>What we collect</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Browsing:</strong> this site sets no cookies and currently uses no analytics or advertising trackers. Search runs entirely in your browser.</li>
<li><strong>Hosting logs:</strong> our host (Vercel) may process technical data such as IP address and user agent to serve and secure the site.</li>
<li><strong>Contact form:</strong> if you send a request, we receive your name, email, site URL and message. The form is handled by a third-party form service once it is enabled.</li>
<li><strong>Newsletter:</strong> if you subscribe (once enabled), your email address is stored by our email provider to send briefs.</li></ul>
<h2>How we use it</h2><p>Only to reply to your request, deliver work you asked for, or send the newsletter you signed up for. We do not sell personal data.</p>
<h2>Retention and your rights</h2><p>You can ask us to access, correct or delete your data at any time via the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Newsletter emails include an unsubscribe link.</p>
<h2>Changes</h2><p>We will update this page if anything changes, for example if analytics are added.</p></div></Base>
